# Docs Reference

- **Delegation gate**: Before performing any step that has a subagent (requirement doc, implementation, verification, commit), check: did the user say "code only here" / "skip subagent" / "do it in this chat"? If **not**, do **not** perform — **invoke that subagent via mcp_task** with the handoff input as the prompt (fallback: instruct the user to switch and pass input). Table: `docs/workflow/SUBAGENT-DELEGATION.md`. Rule: `.cursor/rules/agent-collaboration.mdc`.
- **Workflow order & gates**: `docs/workflow/WORKFLOW_CHECKLIST.md` (short). **Detail & examples**: `docs/workflow/DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md`. **TDD vs DDD (methodology)**: `docs/workflow/WORKFLOW_MODES.md`.
- **Contract (API, DB, ports)**: `docs/contract.md`
- **Requirement/spec templates**: `docs/template/REQUIREMENT_TEMPLATE.md`, `docs/template/BUGFIX_CHILD_TEMPLATE.md`, `docs/template/ERROR_FIX_RESULT_TEMPLATE.md`
- **Requirements list**: `docs/requirements/`
- **Security**: `docs/security-guide.md`

- **Before development**: Complete requirement doc + §3 test plan before any code change. **When using subagent delegation**: the requirement doc is produced by the **Requirements** subagent (Step 1); the main agent does **not** write it — invoke the **Requirements** subagent via mcp_task (or instruct the user to switch to Requirements with the user request or error message). Same for error messages or fix requests. **DB-only changes**: same order (requirement + §3 → schema/scripts in `backend/src/main/resources/db/`); after schema change state "backend/spec update needed".
- **After development**: Run unit/integration tests → record in §5. Then verification (restart + health check) per `.cursor/commands/verify.md`. **When using subagent delegation**: do **not** run verification, §5, or commit in the main chat — **invoke the QA subagent via mcp_task** (or delegate to QA) with requirement doc §3 and "build and restart done"; QA runs verify, updates §5/§6, and **QA performs commit** per `.cursor/commands/commit-on-complete.md`. Main agent is delegation-only. When user said "code only here" or "skip subagent", main agent runs verify and updates §5 and may commit. On failure create bugfix child requirement and retry. For error fixes add §6. When all pass, **commit** per `.cursor/commands/commit-on-complete.md`; when the user requests push (e.g. "push해줘"), handoff to QA (or Release) should state that so they run `git push` after commit. See `post-change-test-verify.mdc`, `SUBAGENT-DELEGATION.md`, `DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md`, `verify.md`, `commit-on-complete.md`. Test workflow summary: `.cursor/skills/test-workflow/SKILL.md`.
- **Todo list**: When using TodoWrite for a dev or error-fix task, the todo order MUST follow `docs/workflow/WORKFLOW_CHECKLIST.md`. See `workflow-todos.mdc`.
- Why tests/verify are not automatic: `docs/workflow/WHY-TESTS-VERIFY-NOT-AUTO.md`
- Which subagent to use (including module-specific): `docs/workflow/CURSOR-SUBAGENTS-DESIGN.md` (§1, §1.1, §1.2).
- **Agent collaboration on requirement**: `docs/workflow/AGENT-COLLABORATION-ON-REQUIREMENT.md` — who does what, in what order, handoffs (including Review, Documentation, Release, Consistency, UX). Role boundaries (no duplication): `docs/workflow/CURSOR-SUBAGENTS-DESIGN.md` §2.6.
- **Subagent delegation (all steps)**: For any step with a dedicated subagent (Requirements, Security, Contract, DBA, Architecture, Consistency, UX, Frontend, Backend, DB, Review, QA, Documentation, Release), the main agent must **invoke that subagent via mcp_task** with the handoff input (or instruct the user to switch if "manual handoff" or mcp_task unavailable); do not perform that step in the main chat unless the user says "code only here" or "skip subagent". Full table: `docs/workflow/SUBAGENT-DELEGATION.md`. Rule: `.cursor/rules/agent-collaboration.mdc` §5.
- **Consistency standards** (Review applies when reviewing): `docs/workflow/CONSISTENCY-STANDARDS.md` (owned by Consistency agent).
- How .cursor rules, commands, docs, and scripts connect: `docs/workflow/CURSOR-AND-TOOLS-INTEGRATION.md`.
